  "title": "API Compatibility Lab — detection quality",
  "widgets": [
    {
      "definition": {
        "background_color": "transparent",
        "content": "**The lab measuring itself** (RC1-611). Six quality dimensions scored from the repository's committed artifacts by `uv run --group evals python -m evals --post-datadog` — no model, no spend. Runs land in the shared eval store, so a number that moves is attributable to a code version.\n\n**Cadence is per run, not continuous**: the weekly sweep (`agent-evals/scripts/scheduled_eval.sh weekly`) plus manual runs. Gaps on these graphs are runs that did not happen, which `agent_evals.scheduled_run.*` already watches — the monitors here deliberately do not alert on no data.\n\n**What is not here**: LLM Observability and cost, because this pipeline makes no model calls. The run records carry zero spend on purpose rather than omitting it. Test health is covered by the fleet-wide SLO (`test_service:api-compatibility-lab`).",
        "font_size": "14",
        "has_padding": true,
        "text_align": "left",
        "type": "note"
      },
      "id": 5621349340345906
    },
